Take an integer as input and print 'YES' if the number is a special number. Otherwise, print 'NO'.

Hint:
A special number is a number which is equal to the sum of the factorials of its digits.
Example:
For number = 145, the output should be 1! + 4! + 5! = 145
Hence 145 is a special number.

Constraints:
1 <= number <= 100

Input:
The first line of the input contains an integer number.
Output
Print YES if the number is a special number, otherwise print NO.

Example:
Input:
145
Output:
YES
\\ANSWERS
import java.util.Scanner;

public class SpecialNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Input
        int number = sc.nextInt();
        int original = number;
        int sum = 0;

        // Precompute factorials for digits 0–9
        int[] factorial = new int[10];
        factorial[0] = 1;
        for (int i = 1; i < 10; i++) {
            factorial[i] = factorial[i - 1] * i;
        }

        // Calculate sum of factorials of digits
        while (number > 0) {
            int digit = number % 10;
            sum += factorial[digit];
            number /= 10;
        }

        // Output
        if (sum == original) {
            System.out.println("YES");
        } else {
            System.out.println("NO");
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
